{
  "claims": [
    "The medication withdrawal rate for the MMG coop_3 group is 89.01%, significantly below the regional threshold of 95% (the rest of the ATS: 99.92%).",
    "In the municipalities associated with coop_3, medication withdrawal rates are particularly low: Camisano (81.82%), Fiesco (76.92%), Izano (74.07%), Madignano (87.5%), Montodine (82.76%), Pianengo (90%), Ricengo (86.67%), Ripalta Arpina (85.71%), Romanengo (89.47%), Soncino (87.62%). The rest of the ATS has a rate of 99.45%.",
    "Hospital readmission rates for the Heart Failure pathway in municipalities associated with coop_3 are high: Roverbella (50%), Moglia (42.86%), Marcaria (40%), Curtatone (37.5%), Porto Mantovano (37.5%), Offanengo (33.33%), Persico Dosimo (33.33%), Sermide e Felonica (30%), Volta Mantovana (33.33%). The rest of the ATS has a rate of 11.35%.",
    "The main risk drivers for patients in the coop_3 group are: days since discharge (weight 1.0), days since last withdrawal of medication C03CA01 (weight 0.6), days since last check-up (weight 0.4), living alone (weight 0.4), weight gain in 3 days (weight 0.4), age (weight 0.2). These data pertain to 5 patients identified in the segment."
  ],
  "conclusion": "The coop_3 group shows a significantly lower medication withdrawal rate compared to the rest of the ATS (89.01% vs 99.92%), with very high hospital readmission rates in the associated municipalities (up to 50% in Roverbella). The data suggest that the issue is linked to delays in medication withdrawal, particularly for C03CA01, and to risk factors such as distance from discharge, loneliness, and weight gain. The intervention should focus on municipalities with lower withdrawal rates (e.g. Izano, Fiesco, Camisano) and patients with more risk drivers, with an emphasis on timely follow-up and medication withdrawal support."
}
